    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0540" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/745</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan (Grew) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 231</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-17">December 17, 1932</date>.<lb/>[Received January 3,
                        1933.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is enclosed a copy of a communication
                    which I have received from the “Manchukuo Representative in Japan,” in regard to
                    steps which the present régime in Manchuria propose to take to liquidate the
                    obligations incurred by the former officials. It will be noted that it quotes a
                    press interview given by Mr. Kiichi
                        Sakatani, who is described as the Chairman of the Commission for
                    the Liquidation of Claims.</p>
                <p>I have not acknowledged the receipt of the letter.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Joseph C. Grew</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d448-a1.xml" xpointer="d448-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
